; One variable: the luminance range of CameraAttributesPhysical.auto_exposure_min_exposure_value and
; _max_exposure_value. The frame is darker than the minimum, so Godot holds the luminance at the
; minimum and the frame draws darker than the default range would draw it. The Physical class
; converts its range in EV100, where Practical converts ISO, so `unit-camera-attributes-auto-exposure`
; shows neither the class nor the clamp.
